azgor wrote:
> [1]: The Helm of Brilliance should also be a light source while worn
> with radius equal to the current enchantment. If the enchantment is
> negative, it should reduce the radius of light from your other light
> sources, but naturally not to less than zero. -azgor

Why am I brought to mind of a metal bowl with a lightbulb screwed into
the top?

The only issue with this that I can think of is whether having a
permanent light source isn't too unbalancing.  The only other permanent
sources are Sunsword and magic lamps, and both are sometimes used
specifically for their light property.  There are fewer useful types of
helms than there are weapons, and using a magic lamp for light is a
novel alternative to using it for a wish.  It also makes oil lamps, and
thus potions of oil, less useful.

What I'd suggest is giving helms of brilliance a flat +1 to light
range, and also making them a light source even if not held
(potentially providing a novel identification method).

> [2]: Decapitating medusa should create a corpse and a head. When the
> head is wielded, all non stoning resistant non-sightless monsters in
> your line of sight should be stoned. It should be as perishable as a
> cockatrice corpse. This is not imbalancing as it would be very hard to
> get this item. You would need to be blind or stoning resistant to wield
> the head this way. Be sure to take it to the bigroom. -azgor

Still too powerful.  Two words: ice boxes.  With an ice box, a player
